        <item>
            <title>0.11.0</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 15:34:22 +0200</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>1100</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.11.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>Jarvis 0.11.0</h2>
<p><b>Your real day, a tidier Settings, and a new way to connect Slack.</b>
This release turns Focus onto your live work, moves every integration into
Settings, and adds a fallback for connecting Slack when your workspace won't
let you install an app.</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Focus draws your real day.</b> The timeline is now built from the
      tasks that actually need you, with an opening line written in Jarvis's
      voice, a sensible length estimated for each task, and your working hours
      set in Settings &rarr; Focus.</li>
  <li><b>Settings, reorganised.</b> Slack, Gmail and Meetings are each
      configured from a sidebar in Settings (&#8984;,), and the Context Hub is
      now a clean status board that links to them.</li>
  <li><b>Slack: connect with a browser session.</b> For workspaces that block
      installing any Slack app, you can now connect by pasting your own
      logged-in Slack session instead. Nothing is installed and no one else in
      the workspace sees it. Settings &rarr; Slack &rarr; &ldquo;Use a browser
      session instead&rdquo;.</li>
  <li>Slack is still searched live and never stored on your Mac.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
